    "body": "Receiver compatibility currently scans every union declaration for each fallback query.\nThe module environment already contains an index for those same declarations.\nThis change reuses that index in `Scope.receives` and `Scope.has_method`.\nThe raw recursive `type_assignable` API and its array-based membership helper remain unchanged.\n\nThe lookup retains the first declaration with the exact union name.\nIt compares exact raw variant names, without suffix or visibility filtering.\nIt adds no index construction, graph cache, or proof shortcut.\nDirect receiver and generic-base matches retain their existing order.\n\nThe fresh normal baseline uses main `0e715dffcb9220479b3b6b5dc2055c81cd990497` and the qualified A19 producer.\nIts cold complete Opus compilation records 16,923,277,666 guest instructions.\nThe raw membership helper accounts for 827,812,963 self instructions, or 4.89%.\nThe native program passes its full reference output control.\nThe offline symbol map reproduces the complete normal compiler image byte for byte.\nThis single diagnosis establishes no candidate speedup or external rank.\n\nCandidate source: `99fda7a649924cdc341f014f52e1d4ab9a6ad0f4`.\nValidation:\n\n- Compiler source and format checks pass with the pinned producer.\n- All 12 selected suites pass, with 94 test and subtest pass events and zero skips.\n- The package adds one terminal pass event and completes in 403.979 seconds.\n- New membership controls pass on x86-64, QEMU ARM64, and WASI.\n- Controls cover duplicate declaration order, empty and missing names, qualified variants, and direct/generic receivers.\n- Imported method collisions, ambiguity, enum methods, union methods, and checked-value refusals pass.\n- Feature census, complexity, and Go vet pass.\n\nPerformance qualification remains in progress.\nThe completed cold instruction pair uses equal-length compiler paths and fixed main inputs.\nBaseline records 16,923,232,536 instructions and candidate records 16,150,097,649, a 4.57% reduction.\nBoth compilers produce identical native output, and the full native reference program passes.\n\nThe original baseline copy lacked execute permission and stopped before compilation.\nThe corrected controller retains the successful candidate run and collects only the missing baseline half.\nThe original failure remains in the evidence.\n\nMain then added struct-pattern and dyn-bound diagnostic repairs.\nLocal merge `3d51e1880abc5025731f23772f1a343fe9c7fcbf` retains both repairs from main `515ddee8`.\nFresh source checks, builds, and targeted tests are in progress before the guarded push.\nThe earlier results above apply only to source `99fda7a6`.\n\nEight balanced timing pairs per workload and proof-cache mode will retain every CPU, wall, and RSS sample.\nThe workloads are complete Opus and checker compilation.\nSeparate allocation builds are complete, but their allocation measurements are not yet available.\nThe complete CI self-tests pass for this source.\n\nKeep this PR in draft until performance qualification and complete exact-head CI succeed.\nNo timing gain, allocation reduction, or world rank is claimed.\nRaw evidence and source identities will follow on this same branch.\n\nPart of #11534.\n",
